                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Under 3.11“Data Management\" may be read as:"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                121,
                166,
                515,
                181
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "“The data shall be housed at the National Level Data Repository (NLDR). Data generated at PACS would be routed, either through the DCCBs or State Data Centers, to the National Level Data Repository (NLDR). All data will be shared with/ deposited and maintained at NLDR, in conformity with the rules and regulations. Given availability of connectivity, all data will be available at NLDR level as at the end of the previous day."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                139,
                192,
                857,
                273
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "The data will be maintained at NLDR and will be available for use by Central Government, State Government and other authorized stakeholders. The data will be utilized to generate various national/ state/ district level reports for Government of India, State Governments, NABARD, StCB, DCCB and other stakeholders, for the purpose of information based effective policy making."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                139,
                282,
                857,
                364
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Till the time of establishment of full-fledged NLDR, NABARD may procure temporary data storage solution as Stop-gap arrangement as per procurement guidelines with due approval of competent authority.\""
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                137,
                374,
                857,
                422
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "The para number and first point under 3.11 “Selection of PACS”, may be read as:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                117,
                432,
                786,
                448
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "“3.12 Selection of PACS"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                173,
                459,
                388,
                475
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• All functional PACS will be eligible for joining the project. A PACS will be deemed functional if it fulfils the necessary condition i.e., completion of Audit of accounts of PACS for the financial year 2021-22. If the selection is being done in FY 2023-24 or FY 2024-25, then audit of the respective previous year will be the cut-off date for audit. However, in case selection has been done in 2022-23 but computerisation is being done in 2023-24, cut-off date for digitisation of legacy data will be taken as 31stMarch 2023.\""
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                184,
                486,
                858,
                598
            ]
        },
